# L §4.5 (tally 2.1.8 R12, #169-f; T's fixes/g3/j3): a row known in a window that holds the cut makes a read a hole only
# where the row would be the one read: v2 governs 2027 on, so rate at law 2026-06-01 is 10.00 PLN (q, qw), and at
# 2027-06-01 the hole (q27). 2.1.7's refcore printed the hole for q.
=== m.tally
model pj
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2027-12-31

source card "invented"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input rate: money PLN

ask q: rate law 2026-06-01 as known 2026-02-25
ask qw: rate law 2026-06-01 as known 2026-02-25 windows each
ask q27: rate law 2027-06-01 as known 2026-02-25

version v
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  rate = 10.00 PLN "c"

version v2
  cite card
  governs 2027-01-01..
  known window(2026-02-20, 2026-02-28)
  replace rate = 12.00 PLN "c"
=== expect
q: 10.00 PLN
  law date 2026-06-01, cut 2026-02-25
q27: ?"date within window(2026-02-20, 2026-02-28) not precise enough for the cut 2026-02-25" (v2)
  law date 2027-06-01, cut 2026-02-25
qw: 10.00 PLN
  law date 2026-06-01, cut 2026-02-25
